# Incident Automation & Tabletop

## Principle
- Automate **pre-agreed mitigation** of known signatures. Do not automate diagnosis of novel failures or irreversible money/data actions.
- Machine loop: detect → match playbook → mitigate → verify SLO → **page a human only if still burning or action is irreversible**.
- Every Sev-1 alert has an owner, a runbook link, and a **safe automated action** or an explicit “wake human”.

## Automate before first launch
- Synthetic probes on login, core create, payment sandbox, `/ready`. Fail probe → page + optional auto-rollback if just deployed.
- Auto-rollback canary/blue-green when error-rate or p99 burns SLO for N minutes after a release.
- Kill-switch / feature flags remotely; circuit-break dead dependencies; shed load; autoscale with cool-down.
- Restart unhealthy pods; rotate to last-known-good artifact; pause workers on poison/DLQ burst; block abusive IPs at edge.
- Cert auto-renew + expiry alert days ahead. Disk/connection-pool saturation → scale or fail-fast, not hang.

## Never auto at 3am (first years)
- No auto **PITR/restore prod**, no auto **mass refund**, no auto **multi-region failover**, no auto **schema Down()**.
- No auto-delete data, no auto-widen permissions, no auto-disable auth “to recover”.
- Those require a woken human + second pair of eyes (`backup-rollback.mdc`).

## Page vs ticket
- Page: user-facing SLO burn, money-path fail, data-loss suspicion, auth down, TLS down, probe fail.
- Ticket: noisy saturation, single-instance flap already self-healed, non-critical widget.

## Launch tabletop (15)

1. **Bad deploy 5xx** — Symptom: error%↑ after release. 10m: freeze deploys, auto/manual rollback artifact, confirm probes. Rules: `delivery-ops`, `backup-rollback`.
2. **Migration lock** — Symptom: DB waits↑, `/ready` fail. 10m: stop new migrate, do not Down(), read-only if needed. Rules: `database`, `deployment`.
3. **Pool / max_connections** — Symptom: timeout, `too many connections`. 10m: shed load, cap pool, scale app down not up. Rules: `database`, `scale`, `performance`.
4. **Retry storm** — Symptom: RPS↑ + error%↑ together. 10m: edge rate-limit, stop client retry amplification. Rules: `scale`, `reliability-crosscutting`.
5. **Payment webhook fail / double** — Symptom: pay success≠ledger, webhook 4xx/5xx. 10m: pause payout workers, do not mass-refund; replay later. Rules: `messaging-integration`, `time-money-locale`, `backup-rollback`.
6. **Postgres down** — Symptom: all writes fail. 10m: rely on HA failover if configured; else fail loud + status page; no DIY restore. Rules: `reliability-crosscutting`, `backup-rollback`.
7. **Redis down** — Symptom: latency↑ or 500 on cache path. 10m: degrade (skip cache), keep DB alive; disable non-critical sessions. Rules: `performance`, `reliability-crosscutting`.
8. **Queue lag / poison** — Symptom: depth↑, same message loops. 10m: auto-park poison to DLQ, pause consumer group, keep HTTP up. Rules: `messaging-integration`.
9. **Dependency timeout** (SMS/map/pay) — Symptom: thread/request hang. 10m: circuit open, serve degraded UX. Rules: `reliability-crosscutting`, `ux-ui`.
10. **Auth/login down** — Symptom: 401/503 on login, probe fail. 10m: rollback last auth change or disable new IdP feature flag. Rules: `security`, `delivery-ops`.
11. **TLS/DNS/cert** — Symptom: clients fail handshake. 10m: if auto-renew failed, page (often not fully auto). Rules: `deployment`, `security`.
12. **Disk full** — Symptom: cannot write, crash loops. 10m: auto-expand disk or fail instance + reschedule; trim logs. Rules: `logging-debug`, `deployment`.
13. **Launch traffic spike** — Symptom: RPS↑, saturation↑, still some success. 10m: autoscale, queue writes, shed extras, cache more. Rules: `scale`, `performance`.
14. **Breaking mobile API** — Symptom: crash-free↓, one app version 4xx. 10m: flag off field/behavior; do not force-upgrade only. Rules: `api-contracts`, `mobile-clients`.
15. **Suspected data loss / bad DELETE** — Symptom: counts collapse, user reports missing. 10m: **stop writers**, snapshot/PITR prep, **wake human** — never auto-restore. Rules: `backup-rollback`, `database`.

## Drill cadence
- Before first launch: walk all 15 on paper (30–60 min). After launch: restore drill + one game-day per quarter.
